interp.Semantics.PrintfArgumentPositions in a column that has no positions.
Measured 2026-10-02 against the shell this dialect claims:
`printf '%2$s %1$s\n' a b` is a refusal at a non-zero status, where zsh
5.9.2 writes `b a`.

-- script --
printf '%2$s %1$s\n' a b
-- lacks --
b a
-- status --
nonzero
